// Was SOUNDNESS QUEUE row cell_typearg_region_invariance_admits; closed 2026-09-23: a callee's `where 'x: 'y` binds its arguments at the call.
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row cell_typearg_region_invariance_admits (tier 2, `admits`).
// AN ILLEGAL PROGRAM COMPILES. This is the hole opened by the callee-outlives
// pin arm landed in this same commit, and it is rowed here rather than left as
// prose because with that arm landed it REPRODUCES on the shipping binary —
// 2026-09-16g measured the same hole and could NOT row it, because on the
// reverted binary the program was still (accidentally) refused and a row that
// does not reproduce reds the queue gate.
//
// THE FACT. `region.outlives.callee-bound-checked-at-call` now enforces a
// callee's `where 'a: 'b` only when the bound's SHORT side is PINNED from above
// — in the return type, or at an INVARIANT position of a parameter. That pin
// test is STRUCTURAL: it walks the declared FIELD TYPES of a struct to decide
// whether the struct is invariant in a given lifetime parameter. `Cell` defeats
// it, because Cell's invariance is not structural at all: it is a LANG-ITEM
// AXIOM recognised by qualified name in sema_auto_trait.cpp. Structurally,
// `Cell<T> { inner: UnsafeCell<T> }` over `UnsafeCell<T> { value: T }` bottoms
// out at a bare, covariant `T`. So the walk answers "not invariant", the pair is
// skipped, and the caller is never asked to prove `'a: 'b`.
//
// WHY THAT IS WRONG. With `Cell<&'a i64>` the caller may NOT shorten 'a — an
// invariant type argument admits no subtyping in either direction — so 'a is
// rigidly the caller's own region and `'a: 'b` really does demand `'a: 'b` of
// the caller, which is not declared here.
//
// legality: MEASURED with rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024. The verbatim twin
// (src/compiler/probes/2026-09-16h-clausearm/rust/r95272.rs, using
// std::cell::Cell) is REFUSED, rc 1, "lifetime may not live long enough".
// Logos compiles this file rc 0 on the binary this commit ships.
//
// THE FIX IS NOT THE ARM'S FIX. Teaching the pin test that UnsafeCell is
// invariant is a different change with its own cost direction (it makes the
// checker refuse MORE), so it is not smuggled inside a priced landing. This is
// the neighbour rule's reason 3, and the number is recorded in the round record:
// all five corpus fixtures carrying `Cell<&` have identical verdicts on the base
// and landed binaries, so the price of leaving it open is 0 on the corpus.
//
// This row closes when the program is REFUSED with a diagnostic naming the
// unsatisfied bound — and closing it must not move the sibling fixture
// tests/logos/pass/bc_0916h_hb_n08_pass, whose `Co<'a> { r: &'a i64 }` carries
// the region COVARIANTLY and must keep compiling.
package cell_typearg_region_invariance_fail;
use logos.lang.cell;

fn check<'a, 'b>(x: Cell<&'a i64>, y: Cell<&'b i64>) -> i64 where 'a: 'b { return 1i64; }

fn test<'a, 'b>(x: Cell<&'a i64>, y: Cell<&'b i64>) -> i64 { return check(x, y); }

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
